{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788491522-R79sRrn1OvqQbApakp2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `url_to_fs(\"dvc://path/to/repo\", storage_options)` will call `filesystem(\"dvc\", **inkwargs)` which is `DVCFileSystem(path_part, **kwargs)`. The path part becomes the first positional argument. In `DVCFileSystem.__init__`, the first positional param is currently `url`. \n\nWait, but actually there are two classes named `DVCFileSystem` in dvc/fs/dvc.py — `_DVCFileSystem` (the fsspec AbstractFileSystem) and `DVCFileSystem` (the dvc_objects FileSystem wrapper). The `protocol = \"local\"` one is the dvc_objects FileSystem, which is used internally by dvc. The fsspec-registered one is `_DVCFileSystem`? Let me check `dvc/fs/__init__.py` and how the fsspec registration happens.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me check what's registered as the \"dvc\" protocol.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ced045f-2deb-4a03-96b6-51f3c49ecc7b","uuid":"f9f4814c-afaf-48e2-84cb-182519a76475","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:12:05.192Z","request_id":"gen-1788491522-R79sRrn1OvqQbApakp2w"}
