{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a06a67648b7313a32f8c1e","type":"tool_result","content":"Here's the relevant code from DVC (Apache-2.0 licensed), with notes below.\n\n**`__init__` signature:**\n\n```python\ndef __init__(\n    self,\n    repo: Union[\"Repo\", os.PathLike[str], str, None] = None,\n    rev: Optional[str] = None,\n    subrepos: bool = False,\n    repo_factory: Optional[RepoFactory] = None,\n    fo: Optional[str] = None,\n    target_options: Optional[dict[str, Any]] = None,  # noqa: ARG002\n    target_protocol: Optional[str] = None,  # noqa: ARG002\n    config: Optional[\"DictStrAny\"] = None,\n    remote: Optional[str] = None,\n    remote_config: Optional[\"DictStrAny\"] = None,\n    **kwargs,\n) -> None:\n```\n\n**Body:**\n\n```python\nfrom dvc.repo import Repo\n\n# kwargs.get(\"url\") is for maintaining backward compatibility\nrepo = repo or fo or kwargs.get(\"url\")\nif isinstance(repo, Repo):\n    self._repo: Optional[Repo] = repo\n    url = None\nelse:\n    self._repo = None\n    url = os.fspath(repo) if repo else None\n\nsuper().__init__()\nself._repo_factory = repo_factory\nself._traverse_subrepos = subrepos\nself._repo_stack = ExitStack()\nself._repo_kwargs = {\n    \"url\": url,\n    \"rev\": rev,\n    \"subrepos\": subrepos,\n    \"config\": config,\n    \"remote\": remote,\n    \"remote_config\": remote_config,\n}\n```\n\n**How `repo` is handled:**\n\n- A fallback chain resolves the repo source: the `repo` arg, then `fo`, then a legacy `url` keyword via `kwargs.get(\"url\")` — the inline comment says this exists \"for maintaining backward compatibility\".\n- If the value is already a `Repo` instance, it's stored directly as `self._repo` and `url` is set to `None` (no deferred construction needed).\n- Otherwise, a string/PathLike is converted with `os.fspath(repo)` into `url` (or `None` if falsy), and `self._repo` stays `None`. Actual construction is deferred to the `repo` cached property, which calls `self._make_repo(**self._repo_kwargs)` and enters it into `self._repo_stack`.\n\n**`_make_repo`:**\n\n```python\n@classmethod\ndef _make_repo(cls, **kwargs) -> \"Repo\":\n    from dvc.repo import Repo\n\n    with Repo.open(uninitialized=True, **kwargs) as repo:\n        return repo\n```\n\nIt opens the repo with `uninitialized=True` (so non-DVC/Git-only paths still work), using the context manager protocol and returning the resulting `Repo`.\n\nNote that `target_options` and `target_protocol` are accepted but deliberately unused (marked `noqa: ARG002`)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ced045f-2deb-4a03-96b6-51f3c49ecc7b","uuid":"085002f1-08f6-46ce-84d2-55b587b41415","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:12:47.222Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":23874,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"Here's the relevant code from DVC (Apache-2.0 licensed), with notes below.\n\n**`__init__` signature:**\n\n```python\ndef __init__(\n    self,\n    repo: Union[\"Repo\", os.PathLike[str], str, None] = None,\n    rev: Optional[str] = None,\n    subrepos: bool = False,\n    repo_factory: Optional[RepoFactory] = None,\n    fo: Optional[str] = None,\n    target_options: Optional[dict[str, Any]] = None,  # noqa: ARG002\n    target_protocol: Optional[str] = None,  # noqa: ARG002\n    config: Optional[\"DictStrAny\"] = None,\n    remote: Optional[str] = None,\n    remote_config: Optional[\"DictStrAny\"] = None,\n    **kwargs,\n) -> None:\n```\n\n**Body:**\n\n```python\nfrom dvc.repo import Repo\n\n# kwargs.get(\"url\") is for maintaining backward compatibility\nrepo = repo or fo or kwargs.get(\"url\")\nif isinstance(repo, Repo):\n    self._repo: Optional[Repo] = repo\n    url = None\nelse:\n    self._repo = None\n    url = os.fspath(repo) if repo else None\n\nsuper().__init__()\nself._repo_factory = repo_factory\nself._traverse_subrepos = subrepos\nself._repo_stack = ExitStack()\nself._repo_kwargs = {\n    \"url\": url,\n    \"rev\": rev,\n    \"subrepos\": subrepos,\n    \"config\": config,\n    \"remote\": remote,\n    \"remote_config\": remote_config,\n}\n```\n\n**How `repo` is handled:**\n\n- A fallback chain resolves the repo source: the `repo` arg, then `fo`, then a legacy `url` keyword via `kwargs.get(\"url\")` — the inline comment says this exists \"for maintaining backward compatibility\".\n- If the value is already a `Repo` instance, it's stored directly as `self._repo` and `url` is set to `None` (no deferred construction needed).\n- Otherwise, a string/PathLike is converted with `os.fspath(repo)` into `url` (or `None` if falsy), and `self._repo` stays `None`. Actual construction is deferred to the `repo` cached property, which calls `self._make_repo(**self._repo_kwargs)` and enters it into `self._repo_stack`.\n\n**`_make_repo`:**\n\n```python\n@classmethod\ndef _make_repo(cls, **kwargs) -> \"Repo\":\n    from dvc.repo import Repo\n\n    with Repo.open(uninitialized=True, **kwargs) as repo:\n        return repo\n```\n\nIt opens the repo with `uninitialized=True` (so non-DVC/Git-only paths still work), using the context manager protocol and returning the resulting `Repo`.\n\nNote that `target_options` and `target_protocol` are accepted but deliberately unused (marked `noqa: ARG002`).","durationMs":10669,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/iterative/dvc/main/dvc/fs/dvc.py"}}
