{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a06a679f84750287c659b4","type":"tool_result","content":"## Top-level imports\n\n```python\nimport errno\nimport functools\nimport ntpath\nimport os\nimport posixpath\nimport threading\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\nfrom contextlib import ExitStack, nullcontext, suppress\nfrom glob import has_magic\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n\nfrom fsspec.spec import DEFAULT_CALLBACK, AbstractFileSystem\nfrom funcy import wrap_with\n\nfrom dvc.log import logger\nfrom dvc.utils.threadpool import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom dvc_objects.fs.base import AnyFSPath, FileSystem\n\nfrom .data import DataFileSystem\n```\n\n`Repo` appears only under `TYPE_CHECKING`:\n\n```python\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from contextlib import AbstractContextManager\n\n    from dvc.repo import Repo\n    from dvc.types import DictStrAny, StrPath\n\n    from .callbacks import Callback\n```\n\n## Type definitions\n\n```python\nRepoFactory = Union[Callable[..., \"Repo\"], type[\"Repo\"]]\nKey = tuple[str, ...]\n```\n\n## Runtime reference to `Repo` in `__init__`\n\nIt is imported lazily as the first statement of the method body — `from dvc.repo import Repo` — then used in an isinstance check: `if isinstance(repo, Repo):` followed by `self._repo: Optional[Repo] = repo`. The annotation-only references (`Optional[\"Repo\"]` in the signature) rely on the TYPE_CHECKING import.\n\n## `repo` cached_property (on `_DVCFileSystem`)\n\n```python\n@functools.cached_property\ndef repo(self):\n    if self._repo:\n        return self._repo\n\n    repo = self._make_repo(**self._repo_kwargs)\n\n    self._repo_stack.enter_context(repo)\n    self._repo = repo\n    return repo\n```\n\n## `fsid` (also a `cached_property`, not a plain property)\n\n```python\n@functools.cached_property\ndef fsid(self) -> str:\n    from fsspec.utils import tokenize\n\n    from dvc.scm import NoSCM\n\n    return \"dvcfs_\" + tokenize(\n        self.repo.url or self.repo.root_dir,\n        self.repo.get_rev() if not isinstance(self.repo.scm, NoSCM) else None,\n    )\n```\n\n## `repo_url` (plain property, present on `_DVCFileSystem`)\n\n```python\n@property\ndef repo_url(self):\n    return self.repo.url\n```\n\nNote: the outer `DVCFileSystem` wrapper class re-exposes these as delegating properties — `repo` and `repo_url` return `self.fs.repo` and `self.fs.repo_url`, and `fsid` returns `self.fs.fsid`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ced045f-2deb-4a03-96b6-51f3c49ecc7b","uuid":"1bdf1f11-e6a7-4475-8c18-dd2476bcb828","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:13:02.488Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":23874,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Top-level imports\n\n```python\nimport errno\nimport functools\nimport ntpath\nimport os\nimport posixpath\nimport threading\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\nfrom contextlib import ExitStack, nullcontext, suppress\nfrom glob import has_magic\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n\nfrom fsspec.spec import DEFAULT_CALLBACK, AbstractFileSystem\nfrom funcy import wrap_with\n\nfrom dvc.log import logger\nfrom dvc.utils.threadpool import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom dvc_objects.fs.base import AnyFSPath, FileSystem\n\nfrom .data import DataFileSystem\n```\n\n`Repo` appears only under `TYPE_CHECKING`:\n\n```python\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from contextlib import AbstractContextManager\n\n    from dvc.repo import Repo\n    from dvc.types import DictStrAny, StrPath\n\n    from .callbacks import Callback\n```\n\n## Type definitions\n\n```python\nRepoFactory = Union[Callable[..., \"Repo\"], type[\"Repo\"]]\nKey = tuple[str, ...]\n```\n\n## Runtime reference to `Repo` in `__init__`\n\nIt is imported lazily as the first statement of the method body — `from dvc.repo import Repo` — then used in an isinstance check: `if isinstance(repo, Repo):` followed by `self._repo: Optional[Repo] = repo`. The annotation-only references (`Optional[\"Repo\"]` in the signature) rely on the TYPE_CHECKING import.\n\n## `repo` cached_property (on `_DVCFileSystem`)\n\n```python\n@functools.cached_property\ndef repo(self):\n    if self._repo:\n        return self._repo\n\n    repo = self._make_repo(**self._repo_kwargs)\n\n    self._repo_stack.enter_context(repo)\n    self._repo = repo\n    return repo\n```\n\n## `fsid` (also a `cached_property`, not a plain property)\n\n```python\n@functools.cached_property\ndef fsid(self) -> str:\n    from fsspec.utils import tokenize\n\n    from dvc.scm import NoSCM\n\n    return \"dvcfs_\" + tokenize(\n        self.repo.url or self.repo.root_dir,\n        self.repo.get_rev() if not isinstance(self.repo.scm, NoSCM) else None,\n    )\n```\n\n## `repo_url` (plain property, present on `_DVCFileSystem`)\n\n```python\n@property\ndef repo_url(self):\n    return self.repo.url\n```\n\nNote: the outer `DVCFileSystem` wrapper class re-exposes these as delegating properties — `repo` and `repo_url` return `self.fs.repo` and `self.fs.repo_url`, and `fsid` returns `self.fs.fsid`.","durationMs":10519,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/iterative/dvc/main/dvc/fs/dvc.py"}}
