{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a06a67d0f0722091e300e7","type":"tool_result","content":"The `storage_options` key used is **`\"url\"`** — not `\"repo\"`. This appears in both methods:\n\n- In `_transform_init_args`: `storage_options[\"url\"] = base_url`\n- In `__str__`: `if url := self.storage_options.get(\"url\"):`\n\n**Summary of the class methods:**\n\n`_transform_init_args(cls, args, protocol, storage_options)`:\n1. If no args are given, defaults them to `(\"/\",)`.\n2. If args exist, `\"url\"` isn't already in storage_options, and the protocol is one of `dvc+http`, `dvc+https`, or `dvc+ssh`:\n   - It splits the first arg with `urlsplit`.\n   - For SSH, it builds the base URL from `url.netloc + url.path`; otherwise it rewrites the scheme to the inner protocol (e.g., `https`).\n   - Stores that in `storage_options[\"url\"]` and resets args to `(\"/\", *rest)`.\n3. Finally delegates with `super()._transform_init_args(args, \"dvc\", storage_options)` — normalizing everything to the plain `dvc` protocol.\n\n`__str__(self)`:\n- Calls the parent `__str__`, then if a `\"url\"` key exists in storage_options, it substitutes the first occurrence of `dvc://` with `f\"dvc+{url}\"` so the string form reflects the original remote scheme.\n\nOther members: `with_segments` copies the path but attaches the parent's cached filesystem via `obj._fs_cached = self.fs`, with a comment noting DVC's filesystem isn't cached by default and that joinpath operations will instantiate it otherwise."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ced045f-2deb-4a03-96b6-51f3c49ecc7b","uuid":"2bb1dfee-bd83-4ddb-ad88-6f92e4858ac1","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:13:08.943Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":1714,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The `storage_options` key used is **`\"url\"`** — not `\"repo\"`. This appears in both methods:\n\n- In `_transform_init_args`: `storage_options[\"url\"] = base_url`\n- In `__str__`: `if url := self.storage_options.get(\"url\"):`\n\n**Summary of the class methods:**\n\n`_transform_init_args(cls, args, protocol, storage_options)`:\n1. If no args are given, defaults them to `(\"/\",)`.\n2. If args exist, `\"url\"` isn't already in storage_options, and the protocol is one of `dvc+http`, `dvc+https`, or `dvc+ssh`:\n   - It splits the first arg with `urlsplit`.\n   - For SSH, it builds the base URL from `url.netloc + url.path`; otherwise it rewrites the scheme to the inner protocol (e.g., `https`).\n   - Stores that in `storage_options[\"url\"]` and resets args to `(\"/\", *rest)`.\n3. Finally delegates with `super()._transform_init_args(args, \"dvc\", storage_options)` — normalizing everything to the plain `dvc` protocol.\n\n`__str__(self)`:\n- Calls the parent `__str__`, then if a `\"url\"` key exists in storage_options, it substitutes the first occurrence of `dvc://` with `f\"dvc+{url}\"` so the string form reflects the original remote scheme.\n\nOther members: `with_segments` copies the path but attaches the parent's cached filesystem via `obj._fs_cached = self.fs`, with a comment noting DVC's filesystem isn't cached by default and that joinpath operations will instantiate it otherwise.","durationMs":4862,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/iterative/dvc/main/dvc/fs/dvc_path.py"}}
