{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a06a67d23d7050bf946b77","type":"tool_result","content":"**Keyword: `repo=`** (not `url=`). The exact line is \"repo=self.def_repo[self.PARAM_URL],\" — `PARAM_URL` is the class constant set to the string \"url\", so *url* is the key in the dvc.yaml repo definition, but the DVCFileSystem parameter name is `repo`.\n\n**Full return statement of `_make_fs`** — contiguous exact lines, shown in segments:\n\n\"return DVCFileSystem(\n            repo=self.def_repo[self.PARAM_URL],\n            rev=rev or self._get_rev(locked=locked),\"\n\n\"            subrepos=True,\n            config=config,\n            remote=remote,\n            remote_config=remote_config,\"\n\n\"        )\"\n\nSo the complete call passes six keyword arguments: `repo` (the URL), `rev` (resolved via `_get_rev(locked=locked)` when no explicit rev is given), `subrepos=True`, `config`, `remote`, and `remote_config`. The `remote`/`remote_config` values come from the dict-vs-string branching earlier in the method, and `config` merges the repo's config with the local cache settings before the call."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ced045f-2deb-4a03-96b6-51f3c49ecc7b","uuid":"53b8da78-637e-4d68-9e81-75c13e11f976","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:13:46.026Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":5476,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Keyword: `repo=`** (not `url=`). The exact line is \"repo=self.def_repo[self.PARAM_URL],\" — `PARAM_URL` is the class constant set to the string \"url\", so *url* is the key in the dvc.yaml repo definition, but the DVCFileSystem parameter name is `repo`.\n\n**Full return statement of `_make_fs`** — contiguous exact lines, shown in segments:\n\n\"return DVCFileSystem(\n            repo=self.def_repo[self.PARAM_URL],\n            rev=rev or self._get_rev(locked=locked),\"\n\n\"            subrepos=True,\n            config=config,\n            remote=remote,\n            remote_config=remote_config,\"\n\n\"        )\"\n\nSo the complete call passes six keyword arguments: `repo` (the URL), `rev` (resolved via `_get_rev(locked=locked)` when no explicit rev is given), `subrepos=True`, `config`, `remote`, and `remote_config`. The `remote`/`remote_config` values come from the dict-vs-string branching earlier in the method, and `config` merges the repo's config with the local cache settings before the call.","durationMs":41067,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/iterative/dvc/main/dvc/dependency/repo.py"}}
